# Pairs with ListedInSink. Production before the fix of #5631: overlapping
# operator deletes of one id shared one lease, which the first to end removed,
# and each deleted the sink manifest outside the grain, unconditionally. A
# capture of identical content republished the id as soon as the first delete
# ended, and the second delete then deleted the republished manifest, leaving
# its row listed with nothing in the sink.
MODULE: ListedInSinkJoinedDeleteSharedLease
TARGET: ListedInSink
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: one delete ends every delete's lease and deletes the manifest unfenced
PERTURBS: DelEnd

--- FIND
    /\ man' = IF row = "none" /\ man = "A" THEN "none" ELSE man
    /\ del' = [del EXCEPT ![d] = "done"]
    /\ lease' = [lease EXCEPT ![d] = "none"]
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: one shared lease, and an unfenced manifest delete.
    /\ man' = "none"
    /\ del' = [del EXCEPT ![d] = "done"]
    /\ lease' = [e \in Dels |-> "none"]
--- END
